<title>USA: Sorghum not a problem with Mexico - US ag group.</title>
<headline>Sorghum not a problem with Mexico - US ag group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. Feed Grains Council spokeswoman said sorghum trade with Mexico was not expected to be a problem despite fears of a de facto ban on U.S. sorghum.</p>
<p>&quot;We're not looking at it as a problem at this point,&quot; Dunn said, because imports were not officially cut off.</p>
<p>Mexico has explained delays in issuance of phytosanitary permits as due to staff cutbacks and large grain volumes.</p>
<p>Grain sources in Mexico City said the government had stopped processing permits to spur use of domestic sorghum.</p>
</text>
